{"abstract":"Recently, number-theoretic assumptions including DDH, DCR and QR have been used to build powerful tools for secure computation, in the form of homomorphic secret-sharing (HSS), which leads to secure two-party computation protocols with succinct communication, and pseudorandom correlation functions (PCFs), which allow non-interactive generation of a large quantity of correlated randomness. In this work, we present a group-theoretic framework for these classes of constructions, which unifies their approach to computing distributed discrete logarithms in various groups. We cast existing constructions in our framework, and also present new constructions, including one based on class groups of imaginary quadratic fields. This leads to the first construction of two-party homomorphic secret sharing for branching programs from class group assumptions. Using our framework, we also obtain pseudorandom correlation functions for generating oblivious transfer and vector-OLE correlations from number-theoretic assumptions. These have a trustless, public-key setup when instantiating our framework using class groups. Previously, such constructions either needed a trusted setup in the form of an RSA modulus with unknown factorisation, or relied on multi-key fully homomorphic encryption from the learning with errors assumption. We also show how to upgrade our constructions to achieve active security using appropriate zero-knowledge proofs. In the random oracle model, this leads to a one-round, actively secure protocol for setting up the PCF, as well as a 3-round, actively secure HSS-based protocol for secure two-party computation of branching programs with succinct communication.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Abram, Damiano","Damgård, Ivan Bjerre","Orlandi, Claudio","Scholl, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-244784"],"event":{"end":"2022-08-18","place":"Santa Barbara, us","start":"2022-08-15","title":"42nd Annual International Cryptology Conference, CRYPTO 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Abram, Damiano"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an algebraic framework for silent preprocessing with trustless setup and active security","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85141672418","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-244784","identifier":[{"id":"85141672418","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-ca11c4c6-844d-4ed3-8398-6d68ac2d2e70"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-171D4854EB0F6DF8A3FF1844651C1DBA"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Damiano","key":"abrampau","last":"Abram","locid":"19a8dc6e-3164-4c94-ae61-b35ed9eb13c2","name":"Abram, Damiano","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivan","key":"damgårdpau","last":"Damgård","locid":"70603eb5-52fd-41e3-8752-15d803c3af5c","name":"Damgård, Ivan Bjerre","name_org":"Damgård, Ivan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claudio","key":"orlandipau","last":"Orlandi","locid":"393c3898-d32f-431e-aea6-ee1e79c535ef","name":"Orlandi, Claudio","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"schollpau","last":"Scholl","locid":"7b93a5ba-5c9f-406e-9190-58367dc70087","name":"Scholl, Peter","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yevgeniy","key":"dodispedh","last":"Dodis","name":"Dodis, Yevgeniy","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas","key":"shrimptonpedh","last":"Shrimpton","name":"Shrimpton, Thomas","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-15985-5_15","isbn":["9783031159848"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"421-452","place":"Cham","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Advances in Cryptology – CRYPTO 2022"},"review":"No Review","scoID":["2-s2.0-85141672418"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ca11c4c6-844d-4ed3-8398-6d68ac2d2e70"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"An Algebraic Framework for Silent Preprocessing with Trustless Setup and Active Security","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-244784","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Digital signature schemes are a fundamental component of secure distributed systems, and the theft of a signing-key might have huge real-world repercussions e.g., in applications such as cryptocurrencies. Threshold signature schemes mitigate this problem by distributing shares of the secret key on several servers and requiring that enough of them interact to be able to compute a signature. In this paper, we provide a novel threshold protocol for ECDSA, arguably the most relevant signature scheme in practice. Our protocol is the first one where the communication complexity of the preprocessing phase is only logarithmic in the number of ECDSA signatures to be produced later, and it achieves therefore a so-called silent preprocessing. Our protocol achieves active security against any number of arbitrarily corrupted parties.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Abram, Damiano","Nof, Ariel","Orlandi, Claudio","Scholl, Peter","Shlomovits, Omer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-195590"],"event":{"end":"2022-05-26","place":"San Francisco, us","start":"2022-05-23","title":"43rd IEEE Symposium on Security and Privacy, SP 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"country":["Israel"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Technion-Israel Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Multi party computation","Pseudorandom correlation generators"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"low bandwidth threshold ecdsa via pseudorandom correlation generators","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85135953921","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-195590","identifier":[{"id":"85135953921","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-7416a245-8ecd-4343-8d0b-cf7c400ec49a"],"keyword":["multi-party computation","pseudorandom correlation generators","threshold ECDSA"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9530234E3FABD9A8AFBBD723D47AB1A3"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"il","key":"technion israel institute of technology","loc":["Israel","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Technion-Israel Institute of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Damiano","key":"abrampau","last":"Abram","locid":"19a8dc6e-3164-4c94-ae61-b35ed9eb13c2","name":"Abram, Damiano","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ariel","key":"nofpau","last":"Nof","name":"Nof, Ariel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claudio","key":"orlandipau","last":"Orlandi","locid":"393c3898-d32f-431e-aea6-ee1e79c535ef","name":"Orlandi, Claudio","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"schollpau","last":"Scholl","locid":"7b93a5ba-5c9f-406e-9190-58367dc70087","name":"Scholl, Peter","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Omer","key":"shlomovitspau","last":"Shlomovits","name":"Shlomovits, Omer","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/sp46214.2022.9833559","eisbn":["9781665413169"],"isbn":["9781665413176"],"pages":"2554-2572","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2022 IEEE Symposium on Security and Privacy (SP)"},"review":"No Review","scoID":["2-s2.0-85135953921"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7416a245-8ecd-4343-8d0b-cf7c400ec49a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Low-Bandwidth Threshold ECDSA via Pseudorandom Correlation Generators","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-195590","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
